From 8c68858d67dc2471d34abe0f16d736711d76a2c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 12:29:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(qwen3-tts): preserve legacy speaker embedding ABI

Keep Base voice cloning on v0.10's native `ref_audio`/`ref_text` path.  The
legacy OVS/VoxEdge persistent voice format remains accepted as strict standard
base64 of little-endian float32[1024]; the worker validates length, padding,
finite values, and exclusivity, then injects the vector into the native
CloneEncoderRunner-equivalent FP16 conditioning slot.  No external speaker
encoder or mel engine is restored, and CustomVoice requests are unchanged.


